// The S.A.M scripting API surface: every function and event a script can use. Written BY HAND,
// because the descriptions are the valuable part and nothing can generate them. It powers the
// in-tool API reference, the event catalog, script-editor autocomplete and the Mod Builder's
// triggers, and tools/gen_api_docs.mjs derives docs/function-reference.md and gui/public/sam.d.ts
// from it after checking it against both runtimes and framework/sam_mp_contracts.inc.
//
// The API is registered identically in the Lua and QuickJS (JS/TS) runtimes. In the shipped
// (engine) build every function below exists in all three languages. Argument order/types and
// return values were read from the C implementations (lua_sam_* / js_sam_*), not guessed.
//
// MULTIPLAYER. A mod's runtime code (events, on_tick, timers) runs on the HOST; scripts name
// players by index, and S.A.M carries each call to the machine it has to run on. Every function
// has a contract in framework/sam_mp_contracts.inc, and its entry here carries the same kind as
// `mp`, lower case (the gate fails if the two differ):
//   host    the host decides. A client's call is refused (one warning, then the refusal
//           value). The function sends its result on to every player itself.
//   owner   the host decides, but the state lives on the player's OWN machine (their backpack,
//           their spells), so the host's call is carried there. A client's call is refused.
//   screen  shows something on one player's screen, carried to that player's machine. Left
//           out, the player is the one the current event is about, else this machine's own;
//           -1 is every player. Most screen functions take the player as an OPTIONAL LAST
//           argument that the function itself never sees.
//   read    reads a player: the host reads everyone, a client only its own player.
//   all     changes a table every machine keeps its own copy of (class and item patches,
//           species resists): runs on the host and on every client, and is replayed to a
//           client that joins later. A client's call is refused.
//   local   answers for the machine running it (its clock, files, music); refuses a player on
//           another machine.
//   any     the same answer on every machine (replicated data, or pure math).
// hostOnly is true exactly when mp is host, owner or all, i.e. when a client's own call is
// refused. The gate checks the two agree; the GUI's "host" chip reads it.
// mpNote (optional) says what a modder needs to know about THIS function in multiplayer beyond
// its kind; the generated reference prints it on the function's "Multiplayer:" line.
//
// Every event carries `fires`: the machine it fires on, and for whom. The gate fails on an event
// without it. docs/multiplayer.md explains the whole model.
//
// Shared constant sets referenced by `values` below:
//   PLAYER_STATS  — sam_get_stat / sam_set_stat
//   MONSTER_STATS — sam_get_monster_stat / sam_set_monster_stat (no GOLD/EXP; DEX aliases SPEED)
//   EFFECTS       — sam_apply_effect / sam_remove_effect / sam_has_effect / *_monster_effect
//   EQUIP_SLOTS   — sam_get_equipped_item

